            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I cloned #41157 and ran `diff --side-by-side runtime/lua/nvim/{zip,tar}.lua`. They are largely the same exact file, with more than 50% of the code being a direct copy-and-paste. This violates DRY to a very large extent. You don't have to make a vim.archive refactor (that is not what I was asking for), but the correct way to go about this is to do `if archive_type == 'zip' then do_zip_logic() else do_tar_logic() end` at points where zip and tar differ (which can eventually be replaced by a `vim.archive.do_logic()` later), and not to repeat hundreds of lines of code.",
